# TT.TICKET_INTERFACE -- the relation-changing writers: change_owner (S-TICKET-023, all
# three branches: Oracle contact, NULL owner, Zitadel names + ids), change_company
# (S-TICKET-024, incl. the event_notification delete/reassign by OSAG login = company 6),
# change_service_host (S-TICKET-015/016, the four locally-guarded label lookups),
# change_service_component (S-TICKET-032, both guarded lookup pairs) and change_type
# (S-TICKET-030/031, OUT event id + UX timeout + ticket flow). Every step records 'ok'
# (plus 'event id set' for the two OUT-parameter routines) or the error code.
#
# Each of these routines writes its audit event directly (not through
# add_status_change_event), so the event's company_id IS compared here (S-TICKET-059 does
# not apply). Events/tickets are selected by fixture ticket id; event ids are never shown.
#
# The empty-side label cases are deliberate (S-TICKET-016: old service label NULL on a
# ticket without a service; new service label NULL for a nonexistent service): Oracle
# concatenates NULL as '' -- a literal PostgreSQL || would turn the whole text NULL.
#
# stop.company 6 (OSAG) is present on neither side; the OSAG contact/login fixtures reference
# it through DEFERRABLE FKs that are never checked (SET CONSTRAINTS ALL DEFERRED, no COMMIT).
# The login's company is taken from its CONTACT: Oracle's trigger AUTH.T_LOGIN_SET_COMPANY
# overwrites auth.login.company_id on INSERT (found on the first live run, 2026-10-21).
#
# First live run (2026-10-21) also showed change_service_host writing a NULL details_public
# where Oracle concatenates the NULL service label as '' (steps 07/08) -> S-TICKET-016
# amended, A-029, translation fixed (COALESCE); PASS since.
#
# ORA_USER=system: the fixtures insert into stop.company, stop.contact, mss.host,
# mss.service, mss.host2service and auth.login; TT holds only SELECT on those.
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=change_owner (3 branches), change_company (notification reassign), change_service_host, change_service_component, change_type on tickets 952110-952112
